{"engine_version":"0.29.3","file":"terrain-slam.toml","toml":"# Sequential (recursive) terrain-referenced navigation — GPS-denied alt-PNT.\n#\n# The recursive counterpart to `terrain-nav`. There, a batch coarse-to-fine matcher recovers\n# a single CONSTANT inertial drift offset over the whole pass. That model breaks when the INS\n# error is not constant but GROWS with time (the realistic case for an unaided strapdown unit\n# during a GNSS outage). Here a particle filter runs the same altimeter-vs-DEM measurement\n# model EPOCH BY EPOCH: at each waypoint the cloud is propagated by the INS-reported increment\n# (itself corrupted by the per-step drift growth), reweighted by the terrain match, and\n# resampled when it degenerates — Sandia inertial terrain-aided navigation (SITAN) as a\n# running estimator, i.e. Monte-Carlo localization against a digital elevation model.\n#\n# Consumed by `kshana::altpnt::sequential::run_sequential_trn` (and its unit tests), and\n# dispatched by the scenario engine as `kind = \"terrain-slam\"`. The DEM is the self-contained\n# synthetic fixture (`DemGrid::synthetic_fixture`) — a 0.5°×0.5° multi-Gaussian + tilted-ridge\n# relief patch over [12.0–12.5, 20.0–20.5]; the track and the particle cloud stay inside it.\n#\n# Scope (honest): the map is KNOWN and FIXED — this is recursive localization against a stored\n# DEM, not joint map estimation (full SLAM). The injected drift ramp is the independent ground\n# truth and every reported error is measured against it, never the DEM's own value\n# (non-circular). A real SRTM tile and a real crustal map remain documented follow-ons\n# (docs/CAPABILITY.md).\nkind = \"terrain-slam\"\n\n# Synthetic-DEM seed (jitters the feature placement deterministically).\ndem_seed = 1\n\n# Track flown GPS-denied: 60 waypoints over an oblique leg (observable north and east),\n# entirely inside the DEM patch (12.08→12.316 lat, 20.08→20.257 lon).\nstart_lat_deg = 12.08\nstart_lon_deg = 20.08\nstep_lat_deg = 0.004\nstep_lon_deg = 0.003\nwaypoints = 60\n\n# True INS drift RATE (deg/waypoint): a linear ramp, zero at the first fix, reaching ≈ 5 km of\n# free-inertial error by the last waypoint — the moving error the recursive filter tracks.\ndrift_rate_lat_deg = 0.0006\ndrift_rate_lon_deg = -0.0005\n\n# Radar/baro altimeter 1σ noise (m) and the DEM representation error (m); combined into the\n# matching σ = hypot(altimeter_sigma_m, map_sigma_m).\naltimeter_sigma_m = 8.0\nmap_sigma_m = 15.0\n\n# Particle filter: cloud size, initial spread around the first INS fix, per-step process noise\n# (must span the per-step drift growth), and the resample-on-degeneracy threshold (fraction of\n# n_particles). Seed drives the deterministic filter / measurement-noise stream.\nn_particles = 4000\ninit_pos_sigma_deg = 0.006\nprocess_sigma_deg = 0.0025\nresample_ess_frac = 0.5\nseed = 1\n","summary":"terrain-slam | 60 waypoints | free-inertial RMS 2947 m (final 5082 m) | terrain-matched RMS 1241 m (final 69 m, 2x cut) | mean ESS 2599/4000 | matching sigma 17.0 m","json":"{\n  \"waypoints\": 60,\n  \"measurement_sigma_m\": 17.0,\n  \"free_inertial_final_m\": 5081.603846962375,\n  \"free_inertial_rms_m\": 2946.5272029857865,\n  \"matched_final_m\": 69.35700526411215,\n  \"matched_rms_m\": 1240.7708323428794,\n  \"mean_ess\": 2599.161462767707,\n  \"min_ess\": 1535.2027068715029,\n  \"epochs\": [\n    {\n      \"k\": 0,\n      \"free_inertial_m\": 0.0,\n      \"matched_m\": 25.48002421295449,\n      \"ess\": 2913.0303175411304\n    },\n    {\n      \"k\": 1,\n      \"free_inertial_m\": 86.15895696136397,\n      \"matched_m\": 78.25467144539844,\n      \"ess\": 2184.0517716174572\n    },\n    {\n      \"k\": 2,\n      \"free_inertial_m\": 172.3168860240323,\n      \"matched_m\": 133.00008690661852,\n      \"ess\": 1849.8879157774886\n    },\n    {\n      \"k\": 3,\n      \"free_inertial_m\": 258.47378669852407,\n      \"matched_m\": 87.34711370393119,\n      \"ess\": 3435.4772149822093\n    },\n    {\n   